From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2000
From: Stuart Shelton <srcshelton@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panthor: declare SCMI perf-domain softdep

Add a one-line MODULE_SOFTDEP("pre: scmi_perf_domain") in
drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_drv.c so that when panthor is built
as a module and scmi_perf_domain is also a module, the kernel module
loader pulls scmi_perf_domain in first.  On Orion O6 with the default
config, reversing the load order means panthor probes before the
SCMI perf domain is up and the GPU DVFS path fails to bind.

Ported from srcshelton/gentoo-ebuilds:
  70200-drm-panthor-declare-scmi-perf-softdep.patch

Signed-off-by: Stuart Shelton <srcshelton@gmail.com>
[ported: applied verbatim from srcshelton/gentoo-ebuilds
  70200-drm-panthor-declare-scmi-perf-softdep.patch]
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_drv.c
index 5bfd5564f..548b91f8b 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_drv.c
@@ -1960,3 +1960,6 @@ MODULE_AUTHOR("Panthor Project Developers");
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Panthor DRM Driver");
 MODULE_LICENSE("Dual MIT/GPL");
 MODULE_IMPORT_NS("DMA_BUF");
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ARCH_CIX) && IS_MODULE(CONFIG_ARM_SCMI_PERF_DOMAIN)
+MODULE_SOFTDEP("pre: scmi_perf_domain");
+#endif
